WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:33.790
Bill Duke, actor/filmmaker/author: Well the
system is set up for the youth and all the

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:46.220
older ones who have survived, all the wisdom
we have now is irrelevant. I just have to

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:49.930
go ahead and say&nbsp;Good luck.

00:00:49.930 --> 00:01:01.940
When I was a young man there was a saying
I never forgot and it was&nbsp;When I was a young

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:17.040
man, I thought my father to be a fool. Now
that I am older, oh how wise he has become.Because

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:28.630
when you’re young you think you know every
damn thing until life smashes in the face,

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:36.530
the truth of the indifference toward you and
all those&nbsp;old&nbsp;people you think are two dumb

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:44.140
to listen to, once you get a couple of scars
you’ll see how stupid they really are, but

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:49.360
you’ve got to be scarred first.

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:53.450
Because us talking, you know&nbsp;They don’t
know nothing…nah…nah…nah…yap…yap…yap.

00:01:53.450 --> 00:02:09.950
Your generation is in the past.But when you
get crushed, and by crushed I don’t mean&nbsp;not&nbsp;being

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:19.291
successful. Ask what the cost today of being
successful is? It’s coming out. So you have

00:02:19.291 --> 00:02:30.480
success but you paid for it and so with that
success comes shame because you wanted success

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:36.319
more than your self-respect.
You notice all these people coming out now

00:02:36.319 --> 00:02:44.990
and saying&nbsp;This is the price I paid. I’ve
been this miserable for all these years. But

00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:57.340
thank goodness I can say Me.&nbsp;They took something
off me. Can you imagine being successful and

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:03.760
knowing the price you paid and choking on
it for the rest of your life.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:11.120
Hey everybody I’m just fine. I’m great…I
don’t care about what I had to do except

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:22.430
when I sleep at night or can’t sleep at
night.&nbsp;Yeah, right.

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:28.210
Film Courage: What about wanting notoriety?

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:44.060
Bill:&nbsp;Notoriety…these days there are people
who will do anything for notoriety. Some of

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:53.910
the things I see on the Internet I say&nbsp;Are
they really doing this?

00:03:53.910 --> 00:04:01.599
He just pointed out to me yesterday [points
to a person off screen] a friend of his is

00:04:01.599 --> 00:04:14.620
an artist, has been accused of it. But he
pointed out to me one of these women has a

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:31.270
website. And she has hundreds of pictures
of herself on the website, the most pictures

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:46.699
that you can imagine, the victim of the due
(who is getting no due process by the way)

00:04:46.699 --> 00:04:48.409
because she said so&nbsp;he’s guilty.

00:04:48.409 --> 00:04:59.039
A friend of mine worked at a company for 15
years and a woman said that five years ago

00:04:59.039 --> 00:05:09.789
he looked at her in a suggestive manner that
made her feel uncomfortable. They fired him

00:05:09.789 --> 00:05:19.820
on the spot (they didn’t want the publicity).

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:37.409
So…these day people do things…acts…this
was on and he put up a selfie talking about

00:05:37.409 --> 00:05:48.409
how he people and how he did it.

00:05:48.409 --> 00:06:09.520
Then there are kids now and doing other kinds
of things online, saying how brave I am. Little

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:25.499
girls going to school (12-year-olds) with
in their backpack, people getting, being famous

00:06:25.499 --> 00:06:35.960
now has taken the place of being of any kind
of self-worth. As long as you like me, I’m

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:43.439
okay. I don’t have to like myself because
you like me.

00:06:43.439 --> 00:06:52.710
When you’re alone, doesn’t that bother
you? I don’t understand how

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:57.871
just having recognition or having people know
who you are or having a million eyeballs,

00:06:57.871 --> 00:07:10.229
I guess that gives you identity these days.
And that’s just the beginning of the next

00:07:10.229 --> 00:07:11.379
to generations.

